  'finale:enemy:maelor_traitor': 'PROPOSAL, to confirm: Maelor, the company’s steward who betrayed it, at the breach, the same man as in his approved portrait and unchanged in build and dress: a deep hood drawn low over a dark leather mask that hides his face, a long coat of deep plum with fine gold embroidery on its hems, a red waistcoat, leather pauldrons and belts with pouches, high leather boots; from one raised open hand a curling wave of cold black ink rises, his weapon. No dagger, no book, nothing in his hands, no emblem of any clan.',
  'finale:enemy:breach_entity': 'PROPOSAL, to confirm: the entity that follows Maelor out of the breach, still unnamed, neither a person nor an animal: a towering shape of cold black ink half again as tall as a man, standing on the ground, its body the ink itself rather than a robe, vaguely like a hooded figure whose long form frays at its edges and hem into ribbons and drips of ink; under its hood-like head, only darkness and two cold white eyes; long thin arms with long fingers, a thin cold white light along its outline like the rim of the breach; from its raised hands a curling wave of cold black ink, its weapon. No face, no clothing, no armour, no weapon in hand, no emblem of any clan. Never purple, violet or magenta.',
  'finale:actor:finale_civilian': 'PROPOSAL, to confirm: a civilian spectator of the Arena of Destinies, a woman of the capital, not a soldier and unarmed: a deep hood and a cloth scarf wrapped over the whole face, a long dress of rust-red wool with a grey shawl over the shoulders, a plain leather belt, soft leather shoes. No armour, no weapon, no emblem of any clan.',
  'finale:actor:finale_citizen': 'PROPOSAL, to confirm: a civilian inhabitant of the capital whose family is trapped under a collapsed house, a man, not a soldier and unarmed: a hood and a soot-stained cloth scarf wrapped over the whole face, a worn work tunic of grey wool under a leather apron, sleeves rolled up, everything covered in brick dust and soot, standing tense and out of breath. No armour, no weapon, no emblem of any clan.',
